      "side": 1,
      "message": "Using `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER` as a sentinel and subtracting orders has a couple of edge cases (here and in `gr-endpoint-decorator.ts`):\n\n1. **Sentinel collision**: If a plugin explicitly passes `{order: Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER}` (or `Infinity`), it ties with unordered components (`order \u003d\u003d\u003d undefined`) instead of sorting before them as documented in `RegisterOptions.order`.\n2. **Non-finite values (`NaN` / `Infinity`)**: `Infinity - Infinity` or `NaN - x` evaluates to `NaN`; since `NaN !\u003d\u003d 0` is `true`, `if (orderDiff !\u003d\u003d 0) return orderDiff` returns `NaN` from the comparator, breaking sort transitivity and skipping the `pluginName` tie-breaker.\n3. **In-place mutation**: `(this._endpoints.get(name) ?? []).sort(...)` mutates the stored array in place rather than sorting a shallow copy (`[...(this._endpoints.get(name) ?? [])].sort(...)`).\n\nConsider validating finite numbers with `Number.isFinite` and comparing `undefined` explicitly instead of subtracting against `Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER`:\n\n```ts\nreturn [...(this._endpoints.get(name) ?? [])].sort((m1, m2) \u003d\u003e {\n  const o1 \u003d\n    m1.order !\u003d\u003d undefined \u0026\u0026 Number.isFinite(m1.order) ? m1.order : undefined;\n  const o2 \u003d\n    m2.order !\u003d\u003d undefined \u0026\u0026 Number.isFinite(m2.order) ? m2.order : undefined;\n  if (o1 !\u003d\u003d o2) {\n    if (o1 \u003d\u003d\u003d undefined) return 1;\n    if (o2 \u003d\u003d\u003d undefined) return -1;\n    return o1 \u003c o2 ? -1 : 1;\n  }\n  return m1.plugin.getPluginName().localeCompare(m2.plugin.getPluginName());\n});\n```",
